WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.688
Last, turn findings into a program.

2
00:00:02.688 --> 00:00:05.025
Read each result before counting it.

3
00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:07.550
Only failures and warnings are findings.

4
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.550
A skipped check isn't
a gap and isn't a pass.

5
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.599
It's absence of evidence,
recorded with the reason,

6
00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:17.688
often a license or a government-cloud
feature that isn't available.

7
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:20.695
Findings are scored with
a documented method,

8
00:00:20.695 --> 00:00:25.838
priority weighs severity against effort,
and the buckets run from P1 down to P4.

9
00:00:25.838 --> 00:00:28.579
Quick wins go into the next change window;

10
00:00:28.579 --> 00:00:31.562
major projects go on a
pillar owner's roadmap.

11
00:00:31.562 --> 00:00:37.961
Both tools' findings are reconciled
against the same SP 800-53 control,

12
00:00:37.961 --> 00:00:41.337
so two pieces of evidence become
one finding for one owner.

13
00:00:41.337 --> 00:00:45.843
Anything not fixed and not excepted
becomes a POA&M item the authorizing

14
00:00:45.843 --> 00:00:49.974
official approves, and drift goes
to the authorizing official too.

15
00:00:49.974 --> 00:00:52.054
Then re-run after every wave,

16
00:00:52.054 --> 00:00:56.212
so a finding is closed by
evidence, not by a ticket status.

17
00:00:56.212 --> 00:00:58.100
Let's close with the decisions.
